      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ### 1. Extract a named constant for the FIFO tag bit-shift \u0026 avoid duplicating `*fifo \u003e\u003e 3`\n\nLine 152 repeats the bit-shift expression `*fifo \u003e\u003e 3` from line 149 (`(*fifo \u003e\u003e 3)`), introducing a second instance of the unexplained literal `3` (the bit offset of the 5-bit `TAG_SENSOR` field in the `FIFO_DATA_OUT_TAG` `0x78` register).\n\nPlease define a named constant in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.h` (alongside `LSM6DSO_TAG_SIZE` and `enum lsm6dso_tag_fifo`) and store the shifted tag in a local variable so the shift amount is self-documenting and computed once:\n\n```c\n/* In driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.h */\n#define LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT 3\n\n/* In push_fifo_data() in driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c */\n\tuint8_t raw_tag \u003d *fifo \u003e\u003e LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT;\n\n\tptr \u003d fifo + LSM6DSO_TAG_SIZE;\n\ttag \u003d raw_tag - LSM6DSO_GYRO_TAG;\n\tif (tag \u003e\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps)) {\n\t\tCPRINTS(\"%s Unexpected FIFO tag: 0x%02x\", main_s-\u003ename,\n\t\t\traw_tag);\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Add automated unit test coverage for `push_fifo_data()` boundary cases\n\n`CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_ACCELGYRO_LSM6DSO` is not enabled in `drivers.default` (it requires an enabled `cros-ec,lsm6dso-accel` or `cros-ec,lsm6dso-gyro` devicetree node), so `./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.default` does not compile `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c` or exercise `push_fifo_data()`.\n\nPlease add a unit test that exercises `push_fifo_data()` (via `lsm6dso_drv.irq_handler()` with mocked/emulated FIFO reads) across the valid range, exact boundary, and off-by-one FIFO tag values for `if (tag \u003e\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps))`:\n* **`raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_GYRO_TAG - 1` (`0x00`, empty FIFO tag):** Underflows unsigned `uint8_t tag` to `0xff` (`\u003e\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps)`) and returns early without out-of-bounds access.\n* **`raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_GYRO_TAG` (`0x01`, lower valid bound `tag \u003d\u003d 0`):** Processes the gyro sample (`MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_GYRO`).\n* **`raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG` (`0x02`, upper valid bound `tag \u003d\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps) - 1 \u003d\u003d 1`):** Processes the accel sample (`MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL`).\n* **`raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG + 1` (`0x03`, exact upper boundary `tag \u003d\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps) \u003d\u003d 2`):** Rejected by `tag \u003e\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps)` (ensuring an off-by-one `\u003e` check would fail the test).\n* **`raw_tag \u003d (0xff \u003e\u003e LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT)` (`0x1f`, max 5-bit tag):** Rejected without out-of-bounds access.\n\nFor example, using parameterized boundary cases in a `ztest` suite:\n\n```c\nstruct fifo_tag_test_case {\n\tuint8_t raw_tag;\n\tbool expect_discard_decremented;\n\tenum motionsensor_type expected_type;\n};\n\nZTEST(lsm6dso, test_push_fifo_data_tag_bounds)\n{\n\tconst struct fifo_tag_test_case cases[] \u003d {\n\t\t/* Off-by-one below valid range (0x00 -\u003e uint8_t underflow to 0xff) */\n\t\t{ .raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_GYRO_TAG - 1,\n\t\t  .expect_discard_decremented \u003d false },\n\t\t/* Lower valid bound (tag \u003d\u003d 0 -\u003e GYRO) */\n\t\t{ .raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_GYRO_TAG,\n\t\t  .expect_discard_decremented \u003d true,\n\t\t  .expected_type \u003d MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_GYRO },\n\t\t/* Upper valid bound (tag \u003d\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps) - 1 -\u003e ACCEL) */\n\t\t{ .raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG,\n\t\t  .expect_discard_decremented \u003d true,\n\t\t  .expected_type \u003d MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL },\n\t\t/* Exact upper boundary (tag \u003d\u003d ARRAY_SIZE(ag_maps) \u003d\u003d 2) */\n\t\t{ .raw_tag \u003d LSM6DSO_ACC_TAG + 1,\n\t\t  .expect_discard_decremented \u003d false },\n\t\t/* Max 5-bit FIFO tag (0x1f) */\n\t\t{ .raw_tag \u003d 0xff \u003e\u003e LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT,\n\t\t  .expect_discard_decremented \u003d false },\n\t};\n\n\tfor (size_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c ARRAY_SIZE(cases); i++) {\n\t\tuint8_t fifo_frame[LSM6DSO_FIFO_SAMPLE_SIZE] \u003d {\n\t\t\t[0] \u003d cases[i].raw_tag \u003c\u003c LSM6DSO_FIFO_TAG_SHIFT,\n\t\t};\n\t\tstruct lsm6dso_data *priv \u003d main_sensor-\u003edrv_data;\n\n\t\tpriv-\u003esamples_to_discard[MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_GYRO] \u003d 1;\n\t\tpriv-\u003esamples_to_discard[MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL] \u003d 1;\n\n\t\t/* Feed single FIFO frame via mock/emulator and run irq_handler */\n\t\tmock_lsm6dso_set_fifo_frame(fifo_frame, sizeof(fifo_frame));\n\t\tuint32_t event \u003d CONFIG_ACCEL_LSM6DSO_INT_EVENT;\n\t\tzassert_ok(lsm6dso_drv.irq_handler(main_sensor, \u0026event));\n\n\t\tif (cases[i].expect_discard_decremented) {\n\t\t\tzassert_equal(\n\t\t\t\tpriv-\u003esamples_to_discard[cases[i].expected_type],\n\t\t\t\t0, \"Case %zu (tag 0x%02x) was not processed\",\n\t\t\t\ti, cases[i].raw_tag);\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tzassert_equal(\n\t\t\t\tpriv-\u003esamples_to_discard[MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_GYRO],\n\t\t\t\t1, \"Case %zu (tag 0x%02x) modified gyro state\",\n\t\t\t\ti, cases[i].raw_tag);\n\t\t\tzassert_equal(\n\t\t\t\tpriv-\u003esamples_to_discard[MOTIONSENSE_TYPE_ACCEL],\n\t\t\t\t1, \"Case %zu (tag 0x%02x) modified accel state\",\n\t\t\t\ti, cases[i].raw_tag);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/266e2cea-a6fa-4b22-8dad-f331f965864b)",
